==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|orv|вꙑ-}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*vy-||out}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|úd}}, or {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*(H)ud}} (Derksen), or {{m|ine-pro|*ūd-}} : {{m|ine-pro|*ūt-}} ({{xlit|ru|Черных}}). In Slavic, the final consonant was dropped.

Cognates include {{cog|en|out}}, {{cog|de|aus||out}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|вы-}}
* {{ru-IPA|вы́-}} {{i|when stressed}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|head=вы́-|cat2=verbal prefixes}} {{qualifier|this prefix almost invariably bears the stress in perfective verbs, but not in imperfective verbs}}

# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[out]], [[out from]] {{gloss|describing an action of moving outside from inside}}
#: {{prefex|ru|вы́-|-йти́|t2=to go|вы́йти|t3=to go out}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[completion]] or [[fulfillment]]
#: {{prefex|ru|вы́-|кури́ть|t2=to smoke|вы́курить|t3=to smoke to the end}}

